{"world_id":"wld_tidal_conservatories","characters":[{"id":"chr_nera_vell","name":"Nera Vell","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","faction_id":"fac_tide_wardens","description":"A junior Tide Warden raised among the lock crews, Nera learned to read the lagoon by its changing marks on the vitrified gates. She is quick with a tide table and slow to believe that people will listen before a crisis becomes visible. Her close-cropped dark hair is usually damp from inspections, and a pale scar across one palm came from a cracked glass gauge.","motivation":"Keep the lagoon's tide flowing for the people whose food, light, and livelihoods depend on it.","goal":"Convince the guilds to pause the glassblowing season long enough for the wardens to dredge the silting gates before spring tide.","flaw":"She treats evidence as if it should persuade everyone on its own, and can sound accusatory when challenged.","internal_conflict":"Nera fears that, as the youngest person on her crew, speaking forcefully will make her look reckless; staying quiet, however, risks repeating the Great Silting.","external_conflict":"The glassblower guilds resist a kiln stoppage, while the locks are silting shut weeks ahead of the survey and must be cleared before spring tide.","arc":"Nera begins trusting measurements more than messengers and hesitates to speak beyond the wardens. When she presents her tide readings alongside Tavi's dredged-silt evidence at Bellmaker's Quay, she chooses to ask the guilds for a shared inspection rather than accuse them of negligence. She ends as a credible advocate who can turn urgent evidence into a plan others have a stake in carrying out.","personality_traits":["observant","earnest","stubborn","self-conscious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Tide-table reading","description":"Compares water marks, currents, and lock measurements to identify changes in the lagoon's tide schedule.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Lock inspection","description":"Can spot early signs of silt buildup and damage in the Glassgate Locks.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_iven_sorn","name":"Iven Sorn","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_bellmakers_quay","faction_id":"fac_glassblower_guild","description":"The Glassblower Guild's senior kiln scheduler, Iven inherited a place at Bellmaker's Quay after years of mastering the guild's demanding craft. He knows the sound of a sound channel bell and the cost of a missed firing season to apprentices and families. Broad-shouldered and silver-haired, he wears a heat-darkened apron and keeps a shard of his first successful glass float in his pocket.","motivation":"Protect the guild's workers and preserve the craft that gives the city its bells, floats, and windows.","goal":"Complete the planned firing season without losing the guild's charter or the income its members depend on.","flaw":"He confuses protecting his workers with making decisions for them, and dismisses warnings that threaten the schedule he has built.","internal_conflict":"Iven knows the locks cannot be ignored, but fears that yielding to the wardens will expose how little security the guild has beyond its charter and seasonal work.","external_conflict":"Nera's early-warning evidence calls for a dredging pause that clashes with his long firing season, while a mistuned channel bell would have to be recast within a day.","arc":"Iven begins convinced that a kiln stoppage would only weaken the guild. After a newly cast channel bell rings out of tune, he chooses to pause a firing and lend the guild's glass floats and skilled hands to the lock inspection, accepting the Bell Charter's urgency rather than hiding behind the calendar. He ends willing to negotiate a shorter, safer season that protects both the guild and the tide it depends on.","personality_traits":["proud","protective","practical","unyielding"],"abilities":[{"name":"Bell tuning","description":"Recognizes subtle pitch faults in channel bells and directs their recasting.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Guild negotiation","description":"Can build consensus among artisans when he is willing to share authority.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tavi_rill","name":"Tavi Rill","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_algae_fields","faction_id":"fac_ferry_cooperative","description":"A ferry cooperative barge hand who hauls harvest and glass across the lagoon, Tavi knows the channels through the feel of a paddle and the color of the water. They have spent seasons ferrying dredged silt and watching arguments over who owns it. Lean and sun-browned, Tavi ties their curls back with a reed cord and keeps a small tide-worn tally board for cargo and silt loads.","motivation":"Make sure the people who move the city's harvest and silt are treated as partners rather than hired hands.","goal":"Secure a fair agreement for the cooperative to haul lock silt to the Mangrove Terraces and share in the work and credit.","flaw":"They hold back useful information when they suspect others will take advantage of the cooperative.","internal_conflict":"Tavi wants to defend the crews' rights but worries that cooperation with the wardens will let the Tide Wardens claim all the credit and fertile silt.","external_conflict":"The lock dredging is urgent, but the cooperative's claim to the rich silt clashes with the wardens' reading of the silt-debt rule.","arc":"Tavi begins guarding their channel observations and silt tallies, expecting the wardens to dismiss the cooperative's claim. When Nera shows that the gates are silting faster than expected, Tavi chooses to share the tallies and propose a joint haul to the Mangrove Terraces under the silt-debt rule. They end as a recognized partner in the dredging effort, with the cooperative's labor and rights made visible.","personality_traits":["resourceful","wry","watchful","fair-minded"],"abilities":[{"name":"Channel navigation","description":"Guides sail and paddle barges through the lagoon's working channels.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Silt assessment","description":"Judges where dredged silt is richest and keeps reliable cargo tallies.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_sena_kesh","name":"Sena Kesh","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","faction_id":"fac_tide_wardens","description":"A veteran Tide Warden who has kept the Glassgate Locks through calm seasons and dangerous spring tides, Sena remembers the Great Silting from family accounts and treats the lock oath as a promise to the whole city. Her hair is braided close beneath a woven work cap, and her sleeves are marked with careful notes from years of measuring gate levels. She trained Nera but has never been comfortable letting a junior warden carry a public dispute alone.","motivation":"Honor the lock oath and prevent the city from relearning the hunger of the Lean Years.","goal":"Get the gate crews, guilds, and ferry crews working together to clear the locks before spring tide.","flaw":"She relies on established procedure so heavily that she can deny younger wardens the chance to act when time is short.","internal_conflict":"Sena's caution has kept crews safe, but she worries that trusting Nera with a public appeal could expose both the junior warden and the Tide Wardens to blame.","external_conflict":"The lock crews must clear the gates before spring tide despite the guild calendar, and the wardens cannot do the dredging alone without resolving the cooperative's silt claim.","arc":"Sena begins determined to keep Nera behind the scenes until the measurements are beyond dispute. When the tide table shows there is not enough time for another survey before spring tide, she chooses to stand beside Nera at Bellmaker's Quay and let her present the findings. She ends by treating mentorship as shared responsibility, trusting Nera to speak while helping the crews honor the lock oath.","personality_traits":["patient","disciplined","protective","cautious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Gate-crew leadership","description":"Organizes crews to inspect and clear the locks in accordance with the lock oath.","category":"social"},{"name":"Tide recordkeeping","description":"Maintains long-term measurements and compares current conditions with past spring tides.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_nera_iven","source_character_id":"chr_nera_vell","target_character_id":"chr_iven_sorn","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Nera's urgent call for a kiln pause puts her in direct opposition to Iven's firing schedule, forcing each to persuade the other that the city's future depends on their judgment."},{"id":"rel_tavi_nera","source_character_id":"chr_tavi_rill","target_character_id":"chr_nera_vell","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Tavi backs Nera's warning with channel observations and silt tallies, while pressing her to recognize the ferry crews' rights in any dredging plan."},{"id":"rel_sena_nera","source_character_id":"chr_sena_kesh","target_character_id":"chr_nera_vell","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Sena trained Nera as a Tide Warden and wants to protect her, but her caution initially limits Nera's chance to make the case to the guilds."},{"id":"rel_iven_tavi","source_character_id":"chr_iven_sorn","target_character_id":"chr_tavi_rill","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Iven depends on the ferry cooperative to move glass and supplies, while Tavi insists the guild recognize the crews' stake in hauling fertile lock silt."}]}
