"category":"physical"},{"name":"Silt assessment","description":"Judges where dredged silt is richest and keeps reliable cargo tallies.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_sena_kesh","name":"Sena Kesh","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","faction_id":"fac_tide_wardens","description":"A veteran Tide Warden who has kept the Glassgate Locks through calm seasons and dangerous spring tides, Sena remembers the Great Silting from family accounts and treats the lock oath as a promise to the whole city. Her hair is braided close beneath a woven work cap, and her sleeves are marked with careful notes from years of measuring gate levels. She trained Nera but has never been comfortable letting a junior warden carry a public dispute alone.","motivation":"Honor the lock oath and prevent the city from relearning the hunger of the Lean Years.","goal":"Get the gate crews, guilds, and ferry crews working together to clear the locks before spring tide.","flaw":"She relies on established procedure so heavily that she can deny younger wardens the chance to act when time is short.","internal_conflict":"Sena's caution has kept crews safe, but she worries that trusting Nera with a public appeal could expose both the junior warden and the Tide Wardens to blame.","external_conflict":"The lock crews must clear the gates before spring tide despite the guild calendar, and the wardens cannot do the dredging alone without resolving the cooperative's silt claim.","arc":"Sena begins determined to keep Nera behind the scenes until the measurements are beyond dispute. When the tide table shows there is not enough time for another survey before spring tide, she chooses to stand beside Nera at Bellmaker's Quay and let her present the findings. She ends by treating mentorship as shared responsibility, trusting Nera to speak while helping the crews honor the lock oath.","personality_traits":["patient","disciplined","protective","cautious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Gate-crew leadership","description":"Organizes crews to inspect and clear the locks in accordance with the lock oath.","category":"social"},{"name":"Tide recordkeeping","description":"Maintains long-term measurements and compares current conditions with past spring tides.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_nera_iven","source_character_id":"chr_nera_vell","target_character_id":"chr_iven_sorn","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Nera's urgent call for a kiln pause puts her in direct opposition to Iven's firing schedule, forcing each to persuade the other that the city's future depends on their judgment."},{"id":"rel_tavi_nera","source_character_id":"chr_tavi_rill","target_character_id":"chr_nera_vell","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Tavi backs Nera's warning with channel observations and silt tallies, while pressing her to recognize the ferry crews' rights in any dredging plan."},{"id":"rel_sena_nera","source_character_id":"chr_sena_kesh","target_character_id":"chr_nera_vell","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Sena trained Nera as a Tide Warden and wants to protect her, but her caution initially limits Nera's chance to make the case to the guilds."},{"id":"rel_iven_tavi","source_character_id":"chr_iven_sorn","target_character_id":"chr_tavi_rill","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Iven depends on the ferry cooperative to move glass and supplies, while Tavi insists the guild recognize the crews' stake in hauling fertile lock silt."}]}
