 open water.","category":"supernatural"},{"name":"Marsh sword forms","description":"A disciplined sword style built around balance and short, precise movements on yielding ground.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_ren_su","name":"Ren Su","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mist_rookery","faction_id":"fac_eel_school","description":"Ren Su is a senior Eel School fighter who grew up measuring each season by the eel catch and the hunger of his school. Broad-shouldered and spare of speech, he wears a dark fishing cloak over his training clothes and keeps his hair bound with a strip of net cord. He respects the Crane Banner covenant as a safeguard against ambush, but believes the nesting ban asks his people to bear the cost of peace alone.","motivation":"Protect his school's livelihood and restore what he believes are its ancestral fishing rights.","goal":"Make the moot recognize the Eel School's claim to the rookery shallows rather than allow the Crane Sect to dictate the ban indefinitely.","flaw":"He mistakes compromise for surrender and uses the old grievance to dismiss evidence that the present season's ban is necessary.","internal_conflict":"He wants his school to survive with dignity, yet fears that yielding even temporarily will confirm that its needs matter less than the cranes' omens.","external_conflict":"His push to fish the shallows conflicts with the nesting rule and with Shen Lian's effort to make the tally-stick's summons binding.","arc":"He begins convinced that the tally is an empty token in a disowned student's hands. When Shen Lian brings the dispute before witnesses at Bannerhall instead of provoking an unlawful duel, Ren must choose whether to honor the covenant he claims to defend. He agrees to send an envoy to the moot and argue for his school's rights there, trading immediate pressure on the rookery for a chance to be heard.","personality_traits":["proud","practical","patient under challenge","protective of his school"],"abilities":[{"name":"Eel-hook sword","description":"A close-range sword method that turns an opponent's guard aside and opens a path to disarm rather than kill.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Tide reading","description":"Reads currents and eel movements in the rookery shallows from years of fishing there.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_qiao_en","name":"Qiao En","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_bannerhall","faction_id":"fac_crane_sect","description":"Qiao En is a Crane Sect covenant witness who records formal challenges beneath the Crane Banner pact. She is small, straight-backed, and silver-haired, with ink-stained fingers and a white feather pinned to her dark sleeve. Her precise memory of the pact's wording has made her trusted at Bannerhall, but she has spent so long guarding procedure that she sometimes confuses preserving a rule with preserving its purpose.","motivation":"Keep the dueling covenant credible enough to prevent another Broken Challenge.","goal":"Determine whether the late keeper's tally obliges the sects to send envoys despite Shen Lian's disowned status.","flaw":"She hides behind narrow readings of procedure when a decision might expose her own judgment to blame.","internal_conflict":"She fears that an exception will weaken the pact, but also sees that refusing the tally solely because of its bearer would make the covenant a tool of rank rather than restraint.","external_conflict":"The Crane Sect's authority as covenant keeper is challenged by the Eel School's claim and by the dispute over whether Shen Lian may present the tally.","arc":"She begins inclined to delay judgment until the sects settle the matter themselves. When Ren Su contests the tally at Bannerhall, she chooses to hear both sides formally and rules that the tally's obligation does not depend on the bearer retaining a school title. She ends willing to protect the covenant's purpose even when doing so requires her to make a public, contestable decision.","personality_traits":["meticulous","measured","principled","cautious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Covenant recitation","description":"Can recall and explain the formal challenge rules and the tally-stick obligation with exactness.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Challenge witnessing","description":"Keeps a clear, impartial record of formal challenges and the witnesses who attend them.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tan_wei","name":"Tan Wei","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_saltmarket_isle","faction_id":"fac_salt_wardens","description":"Tan Wei is a Salt Warden who oversees safe conduct for envoys on Saltmarket Isle. He is a wiry, middle-aged man with a weatherproof coat, a shaved crown, and a small ledger tucked into his belt. Having watched traders and sect representatives depend on the market peace, he values calm above all; that instinct keeps people safe, but it can also leave injustice unchallenged.","motivation":"Preserve Saltmarket Isle as a place where rival sects can meet without fear of treachery.","goal":"Bring the summoned envoys together under market peace and keep the rookery dispute from turning the island into another battleground.","flaw":"He avoids taking a position even when silence lets the more powerful party set the terms.","internal_conflict":"He believes neutrality is essential to safe conduct, but wonders whether neutrality without candor simply protects the status quo.","external_conflict":"The sects' mistrust, sharpened by the Broken Challenge, threatens the safe meeting needed to discuss the contested tally and fishing rights.","arc":"He begins by offering neutral ground while refusing to comment on whether the tally should bind anyone. When Ren Su's envoy hesitates to attend unless the market peace is publicly affirmed, Tan chooses to state openly that safe conduct applies to every summoned party, not only those favored by the Crane Sect. He ends still impartial between the claims, but no longer mistakes silence for fairness.","personality_traits":["diplomatic","watchful","even-tempered","risk-averse"],"abilities":[{"name":"Safe-conduct mediation","description":"Uses careful negotiation to keep envoys talking within the protections of the market peace.","category":"social"},{"name":"Market ledger","description":"Tracks agreements and attendance clearly enough to establish who accepted safe conduct and when.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_lian_ren","source_character_id":"chr_shen_lian","target_character_id":"chr_ren_su","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Shen Lian and Ren Su are rivals over whether the tally-stick can summon the sects and whether the Eel School may fish the rookery shallows during nesting."},{"id":"rel_ren_lian","source_character_id":"chr_ren_su","target_character_id":"chr_shen_lian","relationship_type":"opponent","description":"Ren Su sees Shen Lian as the bearer of a disputed claim that could delay his school's fishing rights, though her insistence on a witnessed hearing earns his respect."},{"id":"rel_lian_qiao","source_character_id":"chr_shen_lian","target_character_id":"chr_qiao_en","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Shen Lian depends on Qiao En to judge the tally under the covenant, while Qiao En's decision tests whether she trusts Shen Lian to bear the obligation."},{"id":"rel_qiao_ren","source_character_id":"chr_qiao_en","target_character_id":"chr_ren_su","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Qiao En must enforce the nesting and challenge rules that Ren Su believes constrain his school unfairly, creating a conflict between covenant and livelihood."},{"id":"rel_tan_lian","source_character_id":"chr_tan_wei","target_character_id":"chr_shen_lian","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Tan Wei guarantees Shen Lian safe conduct on Saltmarket Isle, while urging her to make the tally's case in public rather than let suspicion grow."},{"id":"rel_tan_ren","source_character_id":"chr_tan_wei","target_character_id":"chr_ren_su","relationship_type":"mediator"