 open water.","category":"supernatural"},{"name":"Marsh sword forms","description":"A disciplined sword style built around balance and short, precise movements on yielding ground.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_ren_su","name":"Ren Su","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mist_rookery","faction_id":"fac_eel_school","description":"Ren Su is a senior Eel School fighter who grew up measuring each season by the eel catch and the hunger of his school. Broad-shouldered and spare of speech, he wears a dark fishing cloak over his training clothes and keeps his hair bound with a strip of net cord. He respects the Crane Banner covenant as a safeguard against ambush, but believes the nesting ban asks his people to bear the cost of peace alone.","motivation":"Protect his school's livelihood and restore what he believes are its ancestral fishing rights.","goal":"Make the moot recognize the Eel School's claim to the rookery shallows rather than allow the Crane Sect to dictate the ban indefinitely.","flaw":"He mistakes compromise for surrender and uses the old grievance to dismiss evidence that the present season's ban is necessary.","internal_conflict":"He wants his school to survive with dignity, yet fears that yielding even temporarily will confirm that its needs matter less than the cranes' omens.","external_conflict":"His push to fish the shallows conflicts with the nesting rule and with Shen Lian's effort to make the tally-stick's summons binding.","arc":"He begins convinced that the tally is an empty token in a disowned student's hands. When Shen Lian brings the dispute before witnesses at Bannerhall instead of provoking an unlawful duel, Ren must choose whether to honor the covenant he claims to defend. He agrees to send an envoy to the moot and argue for his school's rights there, trading immediate pressure on the rookery for a chance to be heard.","personality_traits":["proud","practical","patient under challenge","protective of his school"],"abilities":[{"na