ulous","measured","principled","cautious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Covenant recitation","description":"Can recall and explain the formal challenge rules and the tally-stick obligation with exactness.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Challenge witnessing","description":"Keeps a clear, impartial record of formal challenges and the witnesses who attend them.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tan_wei","name":"Tan Wei","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_saltmarket_isle","faction_id":"fac_salt_wardens","description":"Tan Wei is a Salt Warden who oversees safe conduct for envoys on Saltmarket Isle. He is a wiry, middle-aged man with a weatherproof coat, a shaved crown, and a small ledger tucked into his belt. Having watched traders and sect representatives depend on the market peace, he values calm above all; that instinct keeps people safe, but it can also leave injustice unchallenged.","motivation":"Preserve Saltmarket Isle as a place where rival sects can meet without fear of treachery.","goal":"Bring the summoned envoys together under market peace and keep the rookery dispute from turning the island into another battleground.","flaw":"He avoids taking a position even when silence lets the more powerful party set the terms.","internal_conflict":"He believes neutrality is essential to safe conduct, but wonders whether neutrality without candor simply protects the status quo.","external_conflict":"The sects' mistrust, sharpened by the Broken Challenge, threatens the safe meeting needed to discuss the contested tally and fishing rights.","arc":"He begins by offering neutral ground while refusing to comment on whether the tally should bind anyone. When Ren Su's envoy hesitates to attend unless the market peace is publicly affirmed, Tan chooses to state openly that safe conduct applies to every summoned party, not only those favored by the Crane Sect. He ends still impartial between the claims, but no longer mistakes silence for fairness.","personality_traits":["diplomatic","watchful","even-tempered","risk-averse"],"abilities":[{"name":"Safe-conduct mediation","description":"Uses careful negotiation to keep envoys talking within the protections of the market peace.","category":"social"},{"name":"Market ledger","description":"Tracks agreements and attendance clearly enough to establish who accepted safe conduct and when.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_lian_ren","source_character_id":"chr_shen_lian","target_character_id":"chr_ren_su","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Shen Lian and Ren Su are rivals over whether the tally-stick can summon the sects and whether the Eel School may fish the rookery shallows during nesting."},{"id":"rel_ren_lian","source_character_id":"chr_ren_su","target_character_id":"chr_shen_lian","relationship_type":"opponent","description":"Ren Su sees Shen Lian as the bearer of a disputed claim that could delay his school's fishing rights, though her insistence on a witnessed hearing earns his respect."},{"id":"rel_lian_qiao","source_character_id":"chr_shen_lian","target_character_id":"chr_qiao_en","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Shen Lian depends on Qiao En to judge the tally under the covenant, while Qiao En's decision tests whether she trusts Shen Lian to bear the obligation."},{"id":"rel_qiao_ren","source_character_id":"chr_qiao_en","target_character_id":"chr_ren_su","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Qiao En must enforce the nesting and challenge rules that Ren Su believes constrain his school unfairly, creating a conflict between covenant and livelihood."},{"id":"rel_tan_lian","source_character_id":"chr_tan_wei","target_character_id":"chr_shen_lian","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Tan Wei guarantees Shen Lian safe conduct on Saltmarket Isle, while urging her to make the tally's case in public rather than let suspicion grow."},{"id":"rel_tan_ren","source_character_id":"chr_tan_wei","target_character_id":"chr_ren_su","relationship_type":"mediator","description":"Tan Wei offers Ren Su safe passage and a hearing at Saltmarket Isle, but insists he honor the market peace while making his claim."}]}
