dition, power isolation, and mass records during close inspection.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Sail rigging","description":"Works confidently with sail fittings and yard gantry equipment while respecting heat limits.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_tomas_rhee","name":"Tomas Rhee","role":"antagonist","description":"Tomas Rhee is a senior charter auditor stationed in the Bastion Hulk, trusted to take custody of the mass ledger when a yard inspection turns contentious. He began his career investigating a season of ledger fraud and came to believe that procedure is the only protection against a convenient lie. Lean and meticulous, he keeps his uniform fastened even in the office's cramped, over-warm berth and annotates every document in a narrow hand. He is not eager to punish the riggers, but he will not accept an unlogged accusation as proof.","home_location_id":"loc_bastion_hulk","faction_id":"fac_charter_audit","motivation":"Prevent another ledger fraud from being hidden behind the yard's informal customs.","goal":"Complete the inspection and secure the mass ledger before any unverified claim can compromise the audit.","flaw":"He mistakes strict procedure for impartiality and discounts evidence that arrives outside the process he controls.","internal_conflict":"Tomas wants to believe the audit protects workers as well as owners, but his authority is granted by the same chartered system that profits from the yard.","external_conflict":"Mara's report of an energized scrapped hull challenges the records he is charged with enforcing, while the approaching audit deadline leaves little time to investigate Shadow Dock.","arc":"Tomas begins intent on treating Mara's report as an unsupported challenge to the ledger. When she presents a documented power trace and the union's heat-log record, he must choose between sealing the ledger immediately or preserving the evidence for a proper review. He ends by recording the discrepancy as an open finding rather than dismissing it, accepting that procedure must examine its own blind spots.","personality_traits":["methodical","skeptical","reserved","conscientious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger audit","description":"Traces mass entries and identifies gaps between declared salvage and recorded transfers.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Evidence handling","description":"Maintains a clear custody record for documents and inspection findings.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_imani_dao","name":"Imani Dao","role":"supporting","description":"Imani Dao is a Riggers' Union forewoman who maintains the heat rosters and assigns work across the Yard Spine and Mirror Shed. After the Sail Fire, she learned from an older crew how quickly a hurried shift can become a fatal one; she now keeps the duty log exact even when owners press for longer sunside work. Tall and sinewy, she wears a scuffed wrist slate on a tether and carries the burn marks of years handling sail-film tools. She trusts Mara's eye for hardware but worries that a solo investigation will hand the consortium an excuse to weaken the charter.","home_location_id":"loc_mirror_shed","faction_id":"fac_riggers_union","motivation":"Protect the crews' heat limits and prevent the Sail Fire's hard-won safety charter from being eroded.","goal":"Ensure any investigation of the scrapped hull respects the heat roster and leaves a credible record the union can defend.","flaw":"She can become so protective of the crew that she delays action until every risk is accounted for.","internal_conflict":"Imani must balance her duty to keep workers safe with the possibility that silence will leave the union's own mass-ledger suspicions unanswered.","external_conflict":"Helio Tank wants longer sunside shifts, and investigating the hidden hull may tempt workers to exceed their logged heat budgets before the auditors arrive.","arc":"Imani begins by insisting that Mara wait until the roster allows a safe inspection, fearing another preventable injury. When the audit deadline threatens to close the only chance to document the power draw, she chooses to organize a short, logged observation rather than forbid the work outright. She ends still enforcing heat limits, but willing to make the union's evidence part of the official record.","personality_traits":["protective","practical","patient","unyielding"],"abilities":[{"name":"Heat roster planning","description":"Schedules crews against logged sunside exposure limits and catches unsafe assignments.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Crew coordination","description":"Organizes riggers across the Yard Spine and Mirror Shed under tight work windows.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_ezra_noll","name":"Ezra Noll","role":"supporting","description":"Ezra Noll is a Helio Tank Consortium berth manager who handles the yard's scrapped-hull acquisitions and reports to the owners' representatives in the Bastion Hulk. He has spent years turning messy salvage into neat contracts and tells himself that predictable accounts keep the yard funded. Neatly groomed and always carrying a sealed data slate, he looks more at home behind an office partition than among the riggers. The suspicion that a powered hull has been kept off the ledger puts his careful career and his belief in the consortium's stewardship at risk.","home_location_id":"loc_bastion_hulk","faction_id":"fac_helio_tank","motivation":"Keep the yard's charter and salvage contracts stable enough to protect his livelihood and the facility's funding.","goal":"Avoid an audit finding that could halt Helio Tank's scrapped-hull purchases or expose his own approval trail.","flaw":"He protects his position by rationalizing irregularities as harmless administrative shortcuts.","internal_conflict":"Ezra wants to see himself as a responsible steward, but admitting the hull's status is suspect may reveal that his desire for smooth accounts mattered more than honest accounting.","external_conflict":"Mara's investigation and Tomas's impending audit threaten to uncover whether the consortium's salvage records match what is berthed in Shadow Dock.","arc":"Ezra begins focused on containing any discrepancy until the audit passes. When he realizes Mara's evidence can be matched against the purchase records he approved, he chooses to disclose the relevant entries instead of quietly changing the account. He ends facing consequences for his earlier rationalizations, but no longer helping conceal a powered hull from the ledger.","personality_traits":["polished","anxious","pragmatic","self-protective"],"abilities":[{"name":"Contract administration","description":"Tracks consortium salvage purchases, approvals, and charter obligations.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Negotiation","description":"Frames disputes in terms of schedules, costs, and contractual risk.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_tomas","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vel","target_character_id":"chr_tomas_rhee","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Mara Vel needs Tomas Rhee to investigate the powered hull, while Tomas initially treats her report as an unverified challenge to the ledger he is responsible for auditing."},{"id":"rel_mara_imani","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vel","target_character_id":"chr_imani_dao","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Imani Dao is Mara Vel's union forewoman and safety-checking ally; her insistence on logged heat limits clashes with Mara's instinct to investigate alone."},{"id":"rel_imani_ezra","source_character_id":"chr_imani_dao","target_character_id":"chr_ezra_noll","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Imani Dao contests Ezra Noll's support for longer sunside shifts, seeing his schedule pressure as a threat to the union's heat roster and safety charter."},{"id":"rel_tomas_ezra","source_character_id":"chr_tomas_rhee","target_character_id":"chr_ezra_noll","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Tomas Rhee must audit the salvage approvals Ezra Noll manages, while Ezra fears that Tomas's scrutiny will expose irregularities in the consortium's records."}]}
