n the audit deadline threatens to close the only chance to document the power draw, she chooses to organize a short, logged observation rather than forbid the work outright. She ends still enforcing heat limits, but willing to make the union's evidence part of the official record.","personality_traits":["protective","practical","patient","unyielding"],"abilities":[{"name":"Heat roster planning","description":"Schedules crews against logged sunside exposure limits and catches unsafe assignments.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Crew coordination","description":"Organizes riggers across the Yard Spine and Mirror Shed under tight work windows.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_ezra_noll","name":"Ezra Noll","role":"supporting","description":"Ezra Noll is a Helio Tank Consortium berth manager who handles the yard's scrapped-hull acquisitions and reports to the owners' representatives in the Bastion Hulk. He has spent years turning messy salvage into neat contracts and tells himself that predictable accounts keep the yard funded. Neatly groomed and always carrying a sealed data slate, he looks more at home behind an office partition than among the riggers. The suspicion that a powered hull has been kept off the ledger puts his careful career and his belief in the consortium's stewardship at risk.","home_location_id":"loc_bastion_hulk","faction_id":"fac_helio_tank","motivation":"Keep the yard's charter and salvage contracts stable enough to protect his livelihood and the facility's funding.","goal":"Avoid an audit finding that could halt Helio Tank's scrapped-hull purchases or expose his own approval trail.","flaw":"He protects his position by rationalizing irregularities as harmless administrative shortcuts.","internal_conflict":"Ezra wants to see himself as a responsible steward, but admitting the hull's status is suspect may reveal that his desire for smooth accounts mattered more than honest accounting.","external_conflict":"Mara's investigation and Tomas's impending audit threaten to uncover whether the consortium's salvage records match what is berthed in Shadow Dock.","arc":"Ezra begins focused on containing any discrepancy until the audit passes. When he realizes Mara's evidence can be matched against the purchase records he approved, he chooses to disclose the relevant entries instead of quietly changing the account. He ends facing consequences for his earlier rationalizations, but no longer helping conceal a powered hull from the ledger.","personality_traits":["polished","anxious","pragmatic","self-protective"],"abilities":[{"name":"Contract administration","description":"Tracks consortium salvage purchases, approvals, and charter obligations.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Negotiation","description":"Frames disputes in terms of schedules, costs, and contractual risk.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_tomas","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vel","target_character_id":"chr_tomas_rhee","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Mara Vel needs Tomas Rhee to investigate the powered hull, while Tomas initially treats her report as an unverified challenge to the ledger he is responsible for auditing."},{"id":"rel_mara_imani","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vel","target_character_id":"chr_imani_dao","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Imani Dao is Mara Vel's union forewoman and safety-checking ally; her insistence on logged heat limits clashes with Mara's instinct to investigate alone."},{"id":"rel_imani_ezra","source_character_id":"chr_imani_dao","target_character_id":"chr_ezra_noll","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Imani Dao contests Ezra Noll's support for longer sunside shifts, seeing his schedule pressure as a threat to the union's heat roster and safety charter."},{"id":"rel_tomas_ezra","source_character_id":"chr_tomas_rhee","target_character_id":"chr_ezra_noll","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Tomas Rhee must audit the salvage approvals Ezra Noll manages, while Ezra fe