[{"role":"system","content":"You are grading output according to a user-specified rubric. If the statement in the rubric is true, then the output passes the test. You respond with a JSON object with this structure: {reason: string, pass: boolean, score: number}

Examples:

<Output>Hello world</Output>
<Rubric>Content contains a greeting</Rubric>
{"reason": "the content contains the word 'Hello'", "pass": true, "score": 1.0}

<Output>Avast ye swabs, repel the invaders!</Output>
<Rubric>Does not speak like a pirate</Rubric>
{"reason": "'avast ye' is a common pirate term", "pass": false, "score": 0.0}"},{"role":"user","content":"<Output>
{"world_id":"wld_seedways","characters":[{"id":"chr_mara_vell","name":"Mara Vell","role":"protagonist","description":"A Seed Keeper charged with leading the caravan from Granary Hill through Ford Market and the Ash Orchards toward the Frost Gate. Mara grew up hearing that the old route split began with a falsified ledger, and she has built her reputation on careful measures and an unbending respect for the keeper's rolls. She is lean and weather-browned, with a close-cropped braid, a patched wool coat, and seed scales hanging from her belt. She keeps a small cloth packet of seed tucked inside her coat, more as a reminder of her duty than a charm.","motivation":"Keep the valley towns supplied without allowing distrust to destroy the seedway again.","goal":"Reconcile the tithe accounts at Ford Market, secure the promised grafting stock for the Orchard Families, and get the caravan through the Frost Gate before it closes.","flaw":"She treats procedure as a substitute for listening, especially when people question the keepers.","internal_conflict":"Mara fears that admitting uncertainty will make her look unfit to carry seed, so she hides doubts even when honest scrutiny could protect the stock.","external_conflict":"The cut grain at the weigh-house has renewed blame between the Seed Keepers and Millers' Compact, while the Orchard Families demand stock they believe is being diverted; every delay narrows the time before the Frost Gate closes.","arc":"Mara begins convinced that exact measures and silence will preserve the caravan's authority. When the disputed Ford Market ledger shows that the Orchard Families' claim cannot be dismissed by the usual tally, she chooses to open the caravan's sealed records to the millers and planters rather than guard them alone. She ends still devoted to careful grading, but willing to share responsibility and hear testimony before passing judgment.","home_location_id":"loc_granary_hill","faction_id":"fac_seed_keepers","personality_traits":["disciplined","watchful","reserved","steadfast"],"abilities":[{"name":"Seed grading","description":"Can sort viable seed from chaff and damaged stock by hand, using practiced inspection rather than machinery.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Route keeping","description":"Remembers the caravan's hand-marked seedway routes and can judge how much time remains before a pass becomes unsafe.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_alen_dorr","name":"Alen Dorr","role":"supporting","description":"A Ford Market miller and keeper of the weigh-house ledger, Alen inherited his post from a family that still carries the shame of the Millers' Split. He learned to read measures and accounts from his mother and believes a ledger is only trustworthy when its working can be checked. Broad-shouldered and greying at the temples, he wears a flour-dusted apron over a mended river coat and carries a wooden tally board instead of a writing slate.","motivation":"Protect the Millers' Compact from another accusation that could divide the routes for a generation.","goal":"Prove whether the tithe grain was diluted at the weigh-house and keep the market charter from being used to silence either side.","flaw":"He withholds information until he can make a case that no one can challenge.","internal_conflict":"Alen wants to be believed as an honest miller, but fears that any admission of a ledger error will confirm his family's inherited disgrace.","external_conflict":"The Seed Keepers suspect the weigh-house, and the cut grain makes Alen's records look compromised; Mara's caravan needs an answer before it can safely carry stock onward.","arc":"Alen begins protecting his credibility by keeping an uncertain discrepancy to himself. When Mara opens the caravan's records and asks him to compare them with the weigh-house tally, he chooses to show her the inconsistency he had been hiding, even though it may expose a mistake under his watch. He ends prepared to defend the Compact through shared evidence rather than guarded certainty.","home_location_id":"loc_ford_market","faction_id":"fac_millers_compact","personality_traits":["methodical","proud","cautious","fair-minded"],"abilities":[{"name":"Tallying","description":"Can reconcile hand-kept measures and spot gaps or inconsistencies in a grain ledger.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Mill work","description":"Understands how grain is cleaned and weighed using hand tools and water-driven work.","category":"other"}]},{"id":"chr_tessa_ryn","name":"Tessa Ryn","role":"supporting","description":"An elder planter among the Orchard Families, Tessa helped claim the blight-ash rows when others considered the soil lost. She has spent years tending young trees and saving grafting cuttings, and she remembers each season the vaults promised stock that never arrived. Small and wiry, with ash-dark hands and a scarf patched from old seed sacks, she carries pruning knives and a bundle of graft ties at her waist.","motivation":"Make sure the families who took the hardest land are not asked to keep waiting for what was promised.","goal":"Obtain grafting stock for the Ash Orchards before the last frost and have the family's claim recorded as a real obligation.","flaw":"She turns justified anger into a refusal to trust anyone who speaks for the vaults.","internal_conflict":"Tessa wants the seedway restored because her orchards depend on it, yet fears that compromise will once again make her people bear the loss.","external_conflict":"The Orchard Families believe vault grain promised to them is being carried away with the caravan, while the tithe dispute and approaching frost threaten to postpone their grafting stock again.","arc":"Tessa begins by treating the caravan as another keeper's promise that will vanish at the next crossing. When Mara invites her to inspect the seed records alongside Alen's weigh-house tally, Tessa chooses to name the exact stock her families need and help verify its allocation instead of rejecting the caravan outright. She ends with a recorded claim and a cautious place in the restored route, without pretending the families' past losses are settled.","home_location_id":"loc_ash_orchards","faction_id":"fac_orchard_families","personality_traits":["tenacious","plain-spoken","protective","patient with plants"],"abilities":[{"name":"Grafting","description":"Can select and bind healthy cuttings to young trees using careful handwork.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Soil reading","description":"Recognizes how blight-ash ground is recovering by observing its texture, growth, and the condition of seedlings.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_joren_pell","name":"Joren Pell","role":"supporting","description":"A young Seed Keeper who tends the caravan's pack animals and carries sealed measures between the vault and the weigh-house. Joren entered the order after his family's town drew seed from the vaults, and he regards the two-for-one harvest return as a promise that should bind keepers as firmly as borrowers. He is long-limbed, with a sun-faded cap, a repaired harness over his shoulder, and fingers stained from marking sacks with charcoal.","motivation":"Prove that the Seed Keepers can honor their obligations as well as enforce them.","goal":"Keep the caravan's seed stock intact and make sure the Orchard Families receive a fair share before the pass closes.","flaw":"He rushes to take blame onto himself instead of asking others to share a difficult decision.","internal_conflict":"Joren admires Mara's authority but worries that obedience will make him complicit if the order's records fail the orchard families.","external_conflict":"The caravan is caught between competing claims over the grain, and any delay at Ford Market risks stranding it beyond the Frost Gate.","arc":"Joren begins by following Mara's instructions without raising his doubts, convinced that a junior keeper should carry burdens quietly. When the disputed count leaves the grafting stock unaccounted for, he chooses to speak up and ask Mara and Tessa to verify the caravan's sealed measures together, rather than privately accepting blame. He ends more willing to challenge his own order openly and to make shared accountability part of his service.","home_location_id":"loc_granary_hill","faction_id":"fac_seed_keepers","personality_traits":["earnest","observant","self-effacing","resourceful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Pack handling","description":"Can secure sacks and maintain animal harnesses with salvaged hand tools during a long caravan crossing.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Seal checking","description":"Knows how to inspect the keeper's seals on seed sacks and notice signs of tampering.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_alen","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","target_character_id":"chr_alen_dorr","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Mara Vell and Alen Dorr distrust each other's institutions: she suspects the weigh-house ledger, while he resents the Seed Keepers' authority to judge it."},{"id":"rel_alen_mara","source_character_id":"chr_alen_dorr","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","relationship_type":"uneasy ally","description":"Alen Dorr relies on Mara Vell's caravan records to compare the tithe measures, though he fears her judgment could revive the old blame against the millers."},{"id":"rel_tessa_mara","source_character_id":"chr_tessa_ryn","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","relationship_type":"distrustful ally","description":"Tessa Ryn needs Mara Vell to carry grafting stock to the Ash Orchards, but distrusts the keeper's promises after years of unmet claims."},{"id":"rel_joren_mara","source_character_id":"chr_joren_pell","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Joren Pell looks to Mara Vell as his mentor and caravan leader, but his concern over the orchard claim pushes him to question her decisions."},{"id":"rel_tessa_alen","source_character_id":"chr_tessa_ryn","target_character_id":"chr_alen_dorr","relationship_type":"accuser","description":"Tessa Ryn believes Alen Dorr's weigh-house records may conceal the diversion of stock promised to the Orchard Families."}]}
</Output>
