he ends with a recorded claim and a cautious place in the restored route, without pretending the families' past losses are settled.","home_location_id":"loc_ash_orchards","faction_id":"fac_orchard_families","personality_traits":["tenacious","plain-spoken","protective","patient with plants"],"abilities":[{"name":"Grafting","description":"Can select and bind healthy cuttings to young trees using careful handwork.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Soil reading","description":"Recognizes how blight-ash ground is recovering by observing its texture, growth, and the condition of seedlings.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_joren_pell","name":"Joren Pell","role":"supporting","description":"A young Seed Keeper who tends the caravan's pack animals and carries sealed measures between the vault and the weigh-house. Joren entered the order after his family's town drew seed from the vaults, and he regards the two-for-one harvest return as a promise that should bind keepers as firmly as borrowers. He is long-limbed, with a sun-faded cap, a repaired harness over his shoulder, and fingers stained from marking sacks with charcoal.","motivation":"Prove that the Seed Keepers can honor their obligations as well as enforce them.","goal":"Keep the caravan's seed stock intact and make sure the Orchard Families receive a fair share before the pass closes.","flaw":"He rushes to take blame onto himself instead of asking others to share a difficult decision.","internal_conflict":"Joren admires Mara's authority but worries that obedience will make him complicit if the order's records fail the orchard families.","external_conflict":"The caravan is caught between competing claims over the grain, and any delay at Ford Market risks stranding it beyond the Frost Gate.","arc":"Joren begins by following Mara's instructions without raising his doubts, convinced that a junior keeper should carry burdens quietly. When the disputed count leaves the grafting stock unaccounted for, he chooses to speak up and ask Mara and Tessa to verify the caravan's sealed measures together, rather than privately accepting blame. He ends more willing to challenge his own order openly and to make shared accountability part of his service.","home_location_id":"loc_granary_hill","faction_id":"fac_seed_keepers","personality_traits":["earnest","observant","self-effacing","resourceful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Pack handling","description":"Can secure sacks and maintain animal harnesses with salvaged hand tools during a long caravan crossing.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Seal checking","description":"Knows how to inspect the keeper's seals on seed sacks and notice signs of tampering.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_alen","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","target_character_id":"chr_alen_dorr","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Mara Vell and Alen Dorr distrust each other's institutions: she suspects the weigh-house ledger, while he resents the Seed Keepers' authority to judge it."},{"id":"rel_alen_mara","source_character_id":"chr_alen_dorr","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","relationship_type":"uneasy ally","description":"Alen Dorr relies on Mara Vell's caravan records to compare the tithe measures, though he fears her judgment could revive the old blame against the millers."},{"id":"rel_tessa_mara","source_character_id":"chr_tessa_ryn","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","relationship_type":"distrustful ally","description":"Tessa Ryn needs Mara Vell to carry grafting stock to the Ash Orchards, but distrusts the keeper's promises after years of unmet claims."},{"id":"rel_joren_mara","source_character_id":"chr_joren_pell","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Joren Pell looks to Mara Vell as his mentor and caravan leader, but his concern over the orchard claim pushes him to question her decisions."},{"id":"rel_tessa_alen","source_character_id":"chr_tessa_ryn","target_character_id":"chr_alen_dorr","relati