y. When Othric's warrant arrives and the audit can proceed without public recitation, she chooses to inspect the page and seal the correction while keeping faith with the lamp oath. She ends understanding that disciplined silence can coexist with decisive action, and that preserving a safeguard does not require abandoning the person it was meant to protect.","personality_traits":["cautious","observant","wry","steadfast"],"abilities":[{"name":"Archive navigation","description":"Can locate old ledgers in the sealed stacks by their catalog marks and lamplighter records.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Seal custody","description":"Can authenticate an archive seal and provide the lamplighter key for a properly authorized correction.","category":"other"}]},{"id":"chr_ilyan_marr","name":"Ilyan Marr","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_gate_of_receipts","description":"A newly arrived mortal soul, Ilyan surrendered his tally-slip at the Gate of Receipts expecting his account to be weighed and settled. His entry assigns a long stretch of his life to a debt he did not incur; the slip in his possession records the disputed years differently. In life he was a patient maker of small repairs, and that habit shows in his careful way of folding the slip along its worn creases. He is neither eager to condemn the court nor willing to pretend the columns agree.","motivation":"He wants his life accounted for as it was, not made convenient for the offices that recorded it.","goal":"Have the disputed entry checked before he is weighed, so the court judges the account actually attached to his life.","flaw":"He avoids asking for help because he assumes that a system built on records will eventually correct itself.","internal_conflict":"Ilyan wants to trust that the courts can be fair, but his tally-slip is the only proof he has and the weighing is approaching.","external_conflict":"The miscast ledger could send him to the Erasure Wells, and he has no authority to open the sealed account or halt the weighing himself.","arc":"Ilyan begins waiting quietly at the Gate of Receipts, believing that the discrepancy will become obvious once someone compares the papers. When the weighing is delayed but the correction stalls over warrants and seals, he chooses to hand Nera his original tally-slip and state plainly what he can verify, rather than leave her to argue from memory alone. He ends still a dead soul awaiting judgment, but no longer a passive entry: his evidence helps make the account correctable without implying any return to life.","personality_traits":["patient","practical","measured","quietly defiant"],"abilities":[{"name":"Tally-slip witness","description":"Can identify the details on his surrendered tally-slip and distinguish them from the disputed ledger entry.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_nera_othric","source_character_id":"chr_nera_vell","target_character_id":"chr_othric_senn","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Nera Vell needs Othric Senn's warrant to reach the sealed record, while Othric's insistence on certified procedure makes him the chief obstacle to her urgent audit."},{"id":"rel_othric_seli","source_character_id":"chr_othric_senn","target_character_id":"chr_seli_arven","relationship_type":"institutional rival","description":"Othric Senn and Seli Arven distrust each other's offices: he wants a warrant before the Archive acts, and she refuses to expose a sealed ledger without one."},{"id":"rel_ilyan_nera","source_character_id":"chr_ilyan_marr","target_character_id":"chr_nera_vell","relationship_type":"witness and advocate","description":"Ilyan Marr entrusts Nera Vell with his tally-slip, making her responsible for carrying his evidence through a court that can judge his account but cannot return him to life."},{"id":"rel_nera_seli","source_character_id":"chr_nera_vell","target_character_id":"chr_seli_arven","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Nera Vell's request tests Seli Arven's loyalty to 