[{"role":"system","content":"You are grading output according to a user-specified rubric. If the statement in the rubric is true, then the output passes the test. You respond with a JSON object with this structure: {reason: string, pass: boolean, score: number}

Examples:

<Output>Hello world</Output>
<Rubric>Content contains a greeting</Rubric>
{"reason": "the content contains the word 'Hello'", "pass": true, "score": 1.0}

<Output>Avast ye swabs, repel the invaders!</Output>
<Rubric>Does not speak like a pirate</Rubric>
{"reason": "'avast ye' is a common pirate term", "pass": false, "score": 0.0}"},{"role":"user","content":"<Output>
{"world_id":"wld_underworld_ledger","characters":[{"id":"chr_nera_vell","name":"Nera Vell","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_counting_halls","faction_id":"fac_scribes_order","description":"A junior scribe of the Order, Nera has spent her short tenure copying other clerks' neat certainties into the ledgers. She noticed that the mortal Ilyan Marr's final years were entered in the column for an unearned debt, though the source tally-slip records a different account. Nera is narrow-shouldered, ink-stained at the cuffs, and keeps a chipped nib tucked behind one ear. She learned to make herself unobtrusive in a room where senior clerks treat a corrected line as an accusation.","motivation":"She wants the written account to reflect what happened, even when correcting it exposes the office that certified the error.","goal":"Carry Ilyan Marr's correction through the counting-houses and obtain the three seals before he is weighed.","flaw":"She mistakes solitary accuracy for sufficient courage and initially withholds evidence until she can make her case unanswerable.","internal_conflict":"Nera fears that speaking without perfect proof will make her look like the careless junior who caused the miscast tally.","external_conflict":"The Weighers will not delay Ilyan's weighing without a warrant, the Lamplighters require that warrant to open his sealed ledger, and the correction cannot stand without all three keys.","arc":"Nera begins by quietly checking the discrepancy and waiting for a flawless case. When Ilyan reaches the Hall of Scales and the sealed ledger remains inaccessible, she chooses to name the Order's own transcription error in front of the weigher and asks Seli to risk her post by verifying the page. She ends willing to put her name beside an imperfectly defended truth, rather than let procedural delay turn a correctable account into an irreversible judgment.","personality_traits":["meticulous","dry-witted","self-effacing","stubborn"],"abilities":[{"name":"Column memory","description":"Can recall the layout and wording of ledger entries she has copied, helping her spot transpositions and omissions.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Formal petitioning","description":"Knows the Order's filing conventions well enough to route a correction through its offices without losing the record.","category":"other"}]},{"id":"chr_othric_senn","name":"Othric Senn","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_hall_of_scales","faction_id":"fac_weighers","description":"A senior officer of the Collegium of Weighers, Othric certifies balances with a ceremonial calm that makes every decision sound inevitable. During the rise in miscast tallies, he has defended the Collegium by insisting that a ledger is the only evidence the court can weigh. He wears a dark, carefully brushed robe and keeps his warrant seals aligned by size. His opposition to Nera is not a secret scheme: he believes that admitting uncertainty in one case will undermine every certified balance.","motivation":"He wants the weighing court to remain credible and fears another season of disorder like the War of the Wrong Column.","goal":"Proceed with Ilyan's scheduled weighing unless a properly warranted correction is presented.","flaw":"He treats institutional consistency as proof of fairness, even when the record itself is suspect.","internal_conflict":"Othric knows that a process can preserve its authority while doing wrong, but fears that acknowledging a flawed certification will make every judgment appear arbitrary.","external_conflict":"Nera's evidence challenges a balance his office is expected to certify, while the Lamplighters refuse to open the sealed ledger without his warrant.","arc":"Othric begins convinced that delay and exception are more dangerous than a disputed entry. When Nera identifies the Order's source record and accepts public responsibility for its transcription, he must choose between protecting the Collegium's appearance and issuing the warrant needed for a three-key audit. He grants it, ending with a narrower but more honest view of authority: certification is a duty to test the account, not merely to defend the seal.","personality_traits":["formal","patient","proud","risk-averse"],"abilities":[{"name":"Balance certification","description":"Can interpret the Collegium's weighing records and determine what evidence is required before a balance may be certified.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Warrant authority","description":"Can issue the Collegium's warrant that permits a sealed ledger to be examined for audit.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_seli_arven","name":"Seli Arven","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_lamp_archive","faction_id":"fac_lamplighters","description":"A Lamplighter Kin keeper, Seli tends the sealed stacks with a steady hand and an exacting sense of what must remain unread. She remembers the Lamp Seal as a safeguard against one office rewriting another's work, not as permission to hide a mistake forever. Small and silver-haired, she wears a brass lamp-hook at her belt and keeps her sleeves free of wax. The oath against reading a sealed page aloud has shaped her life: she knows that opening a record without authority could cost her lamp and post.","motivation":"She wants the Archive's safeguards to protect the dead without becoming an excuse to abandon them to a known error.","goal":"Verify Ilyan's sealed ledger under a valid weigher's warrant and provide the lamplighter key without reading the page aloud.","flaw":"She relies so heavily on the letter of the oath that she can confuse silence with neutrality.","internal_conflict":"Seli fears losing her lamp and post, yet fears more that her caution has made the Archive complicit in preventable harm.","external_conflict":"The sealed ledgers cannot be opened for Nera's audit without a weigher's warrant, and reading a page aloud would cost Seli her position.","arc":"Seli begins protecting the Archive by refusing even to discuss the sealed entry. When Othric's warrant arrives and the audit can proceed without public recitation, she chooses to inspect the page and seal the correction while keeping faith with the lamp oath. She ends understanding that disciplined silence can coexist with decisive action, and that preserving a safeguard does not require abandoning the person it was meant to protect.","personality_traits":["cautious","observant","wry","steadfast"],"abilities":[{"name":"Archive navigation","description":"Can locate old ledgers in the sealed stacks by their catalog marks and lamplighter records.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Seal custody","description":"Can authenticate an archive seal and provide the lamplighter key for a properly authorized correction.","category":"other"}]},{"id":"chr_ilyan_marr","name":"Ilyan Marr","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_gate_of_receipts","description":"A newly arrived mortal soul, Ilyan surrendered his tally-slip at the Gate of Receipts expecting his account to be weighed and settled. His entry assigns a long stretch of his life to a debt he did not incur; the slip in his possession records the disputed years differently. In life he was a patient maker of small repairs, and that habit shows in his careful way of folding the slip along its worn creases. He is neither eager to condemn the court nor willing to pretend the columns agree.","motivation":"He wants his life accounted for as it was, not made convenient for the offices that recorded it.","goal":"Have the disputed entry checked before he is weighed, so the court judges the account actually attached to his life.","flaw":"He avoids asking for help because he assumes that a system built on records will eventually correct itself.","internal_conflict":"Ilyan wants to trust that the courts can be fair, but his tally-slip is the only proof he has and the weighing is approaching.","external_conflict":"The miscast ledger could send him to the Erasure Wells, and he has no authority to open the sealed account or halt the weighing himself.","arc":"Ilyan begins waiting quietly at the Gate of Receipts, believing that the discrepancy will become obvious once someone compares the papers. When the weighing is delayed but the correction stalls over warrants and seals, he chooses to hand Nera his original tally-slip and state plainly what he can verify, rather than leave her to argue from memory alone. He ends still a dead soul awaiting judgment, but no longer a passive entry: his evidence helps make the account correctable without implying any return to life.","personality_traits":["patient","practical","measured","quietly defiant"],"abilities":[{"name":"Tally-slip witness","description":"Can identify the details on his surrendered tally-slip and distinguish them from the disputed ledger entry.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_nera_othric","source_character_id":"chr_nera_vell","target_character_id":"chr_othric_senn","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Nera Vell needs Othric Senn's warrant to reach the sealed record, while Othric's insistence on certified procedure makes him the chief obstacle to her urgent audit."},{"id":"rel_othric_seli","source_character_id":"chr_othric_senn","target_character_id":"chr_seli_arven","relationship_type":"institutional rival","description":"Othric Senn and Seli Arven distrust each other's offices: he wants a warrant before the Archive acts, and she refuses to expose a sealed ledger without one."},{"id":"rel_ilyan_nera","source_character_id":"chr_ilyan_marr","target_character_id":"chr_nera_vell","relationship_type":"witness and advocate","description":"Ilyan Marr entrusts Nera Vell with his tally-slip, making her responsible for carrying his evidence through a court that can judge his account but cannot return him to life."},{"id":"rel_nera_seli","source_character_id":"chr_nera_vell","target_character_id":"chr_seli_arven","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Nera Vell's request tests Seli Arven's loyalty to the Lamp Oath; their alliance depends on verifying the sealed page without reading it aloud."}]}
</Output>
