{"world_id":"wld_bellwether","characters":[{"id":"chr_mara_vell","name":"Mara Vell","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_founder_row","faction_id":"fac_bell_founders","description":"A young bell-founder's apprentice raised among Founder Row's soot-blackened workshops, Mara learned to judge a casting by its cooling note before she could read a ledger. Her late mother registered her name at the Salt Chapel, and Mara keeps the token tucked beneath her collar, answering to its carved notch whenever fog gathers. She is spare and quick-handed, with burn scars on two fingers, cropped dark hair, and a brass founder's gauge hanging from her belt. She heard the unmarked ninth pattern during a storm-bell test and recognizes in it a rhythm that no Collegium record accounts for.","motivation":"Prove that the strange ring has a cause that can be understood without sacrificing the city's people to silence.","goal":"Trace the unmarked pattern to its source before the Parish Watch's writ stills the wall's bells ahead of the next fog.","flaw":"She treats every problem as a technical puzzle and withholds what she knows until she can prove it beyond doubt.","internal_conflict":"Mara fears that exposing the pattern will reveal her own imperfect work and cost her the only craft and community she has ever known.","external_conflict":"The watch threatens to silence the storm-bells, while the Collegium denies any unmarked casting and restricts her access to its records.","arc":"Mara begins convinced that proof must come before trust. When the watch presents its stilling writ at the Sea-Wall Belfry and she must choose between hiding her incomplete measurements or warning the others, she shares them with the people she distrusts. By the end, she accepts responsibility for investigating the ring openly, even without certainty, and no longer lets fear of a flawed reputation decide what the city gets to know.","personality_traits":["observant","stubborn","exacting","protective"],"abilities":[{"name":"Read the ring","description":"Can identify subtle differences in a bell's tone and use its founder's mark and resonance to narrow down how and where it was made.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Foundry hand","description":"Skilled at inspecting bronze castings, reading cooling flaws, and making careful repairs with the tools of a bell-founder's workshop.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_orrin_kest","name":"Orrin Kest","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_bailiffs_stairs","faction_id":"fac_parish_watch","description":"A senior warden of the Parish Watch, Orrin Kest has spent years enforcing the silence laws and reading writs at Bailiff's Stairs. He grew up in the aftermath of the Lost Parish, raised by a family who believed that a name spoken carelessly in fog could erase a whole household. He is broad-shouldered and meticulously dressed in a high-collared coat, with a salt-stained name-token and a polished brass seal-case at his side. Orrin does not hate the founders; he believes their pride in the bells has made them reckless with lives that the watch must protect.","motivation":"Prevent another parish from being lost to the Chiming, even if safety requires severe restrictions.","goal":"Have the nine storm-bells stilled by writ until the threat of the unmarked ring is resolved.","flaw":"He confuses control with protection and treats disagreement as a danger to contain.","internal_conflict":"Orrin wants to honor the people taken in the Lost Parish, but fears that any compromise with uncertainty will repeat that catastrophe.","external_conflict":"The bell-founder apprentice challenges his order to silence the wall, while the fog brokers' name-debts undermine the watch's authority in the parish.","arc":"Orrin begins certain that only immediate silence can protect the city. When Mara's measurements show that the bells' pattern may be warning of a specific danger rather than causing it, he must choose whether to enforce his writ without hearing her out. He delays the order long enough for her to investigate, accepting public responsibility for the risk; by the end, he still values caution but no longer mistakes unquestioned control for safety.","personality_traits":["disciplined","cautious","unyielding","dutiful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Writ keeper","description":"Knows the parish's silence laws and procedures for issuing and enforcing orders concerning the bells.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Watch command","description":"Can organize wardens, secure a public reading, and hold a tense crowd to order without raising his voice.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_sella_quill","name":"Sella Quill","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_fogmarket","faction_id":"fac_fog_brokers","description":"A licensed Fog Broker who works beneath the Fogmarket's oil lamps, Sella Quill trades in secrets and name-debts under the charter. She entered the trade after the Chiming took her brother's spoken name; the salt registry preserves his entry, but she has never found anyone who remembers him as she did. Sella is compact and sharply dressed, with a net of tiny market tokens sewn inside her cuffs and a narrow veil she lowers when the fog thickens. She has a talent for discovering who owes whom, and she knows that the unmarked ring has stirred buyers and sellers into unusually careful silence.","motivation":"Keep the Fog Brokers' charter intact so the market can continue managing dangerous debts in one place.","goal":"Find out who is trading information about the unmarked ring before the watch uses the panic to close the Fogmarket.","flaw":"She turns every bond into a bargain and assumes that help freely given will become a debt.","internal_conflict":"Sella wants to protect people from losing their names, but fears that acting without payment will leave her with no leverage when the market is threatened.","external_conflict":"The Parish Watch calls the brokers' name-debts extortion and may shut the market; Mara's investigation risks exposing a source Sella has promised to protect.","arc":"Sella begins by offering Mara only information in exchange for a valuable secret. When a watch patrol arrives at the Fogmarket seeking the source of the ring's rumors, Sella must choose whether to name Mara as the source or risk her own charter by redirecting the patrol. She protects Mara without demanding a debt, and ends willing to use her market's knowledge as a public safeguard rather than only as private leverage.","personality_traits":["wry","calculating","resourceful","guarded"],"abilities":[{"name":"Market listening","description":"Can piece together rumors and obligations from careful conversations with traders who would not speak openly to the watch.","category":"social"},{"name":"Debt ledger","description":"Remembers the terms and connections behind many name-debts traded under the Fog Brokers' charter.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_ada_rook","name":"Ada Rook","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_salt_chapel","description":"The Salt Chapel's registrar, Ada Rook maintains the tablets on which every citizen's name is kept against the fog. She took up the office after the death of her predecessor and has spent years repairing entries blurred by damp air and careless hands. Tall and stooped, with silver hair braided close to her head, she wears a plain apron dusted white with salt and carries a narrow slate for recording marks instead of speaking names aloud. Ada believes the registry is a promise made by the living to remember one another, not merely a safeguard against the Chiming.","motivation":"Preserve the integrity of the salt registry and the dignity of those whose names it holds.","goal":"Discover whether the unmarked ring has disturbed a registered name before the next fog reaches the chapel.","flaw":"She clings to procedure even when delay leaves people without the help they need.","internal_conflict":"Ada fears that acting on uncertain evidence will damage the registry, yet knows that silence can abandon the very citizens it exists to protect.","external_conflict":"The watch's proposed stilling order and the brokers' name-debts both threaten to make the registry a tool of control rather than communal memory.","arc":"Ada begins by refusing to alter or reveal any registry entry without a complete formal record. When Mara brings her a name-token whose salt entry has begun to blur after the strange ring, Ada must choose between waiting for official authorization and sharing what she knows before the fog arrives. She opens the relevant record to Mara and Orrin, accepting that careful cooperation is not the same as careless tampering; by the end, she keeps the registry's safeguards while making its warnings available in time to matter.","personality_traits":["patient","scrupulous","compassionate","reserved"],"abilities":[{"name":"Salt registrar","description":"Can maintain the chapel's name entries and recognize when salt, handwriting, or a citizen's token shows signs of disturbance.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Silent protocol","description":"Communicates names and instructions through established signs and written marks when fog makes speech unsafe.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_orrin","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","target_character_id":"chr_orrin_kest","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Mara Vell's effort to investigate the unmarked ring directly opposes Orrin Kest's order to still the storm-bells, forcing them to decide whether evidence or precaution should guide the parish."},{"id":"rel_orrin_mara","source_character_id":"chr_orrin_kest","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","relationship_type":"authority","description":"Orrin Kest has the power to enforce a writ against Mara Vell, while her knowledge of the bells makes her the witness he must either silence or hear."},{"id":"rel_mara_sella","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","target_character_id":"chr_sella_quill","relationship_type":"uneasy ally","description":"Sella Quill gives Mara Vell access to Fogmarket rumors, but their alliance is strained by Sella's habit of treating information as a debt."},{"id":"rel_ada_mara","source_character_id":"chr_ada_rook","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Ada Rook teaches Mara Vell how the salt registry protects names and challenges her to consider who could be harmed by keeping evidence private."},{"id":"rel_ada_orrin","source_character_id":"chr_ada_rook","target_character_id":"chr_orrin_kest","relationship_type":"opponent","description":"Ada Rook resists Orrin Kest's attempt to make the registry serve the watch's control, while he fears her caution about procedure will leave the parish exposed."}]}
</Output>
