ing her out. He delays the order long enough for her to investigate, accepting public responsibility for the risk; by the end, he still values caution but no longer mistakes unquestioned control for safety.","personality_traits":["disciplined","cautious","unyielding","dutiful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Writ keeper","description":"Knows the parish's silence laws and procedures for issuing and enforcing orders concerning the bells.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Watch command","description":"Can organize wardens, secure a public reading, and hold a tense crowd to order without raising his voice.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_sella_quill","name":"Sella Quill","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_fogmarket","faction_id":"fac_fog_brokers","description":"A licensed Fog Broker who works beneath the Fogmarket's oil lamps, Sella Quill trades in secrets and name-debts under the charter. She entered the trade after the Chiming took her brother's spoken name; the salt registry preserves his entry, but she has never found anyone who remembers him as she did. Sella is compact and sharply dressed, with a net of tiny market tokens sewn inside her cuffs and a narrow veil she lowers when the fog thickens. She has a talent for discovering who owes whom, and she knows that the unmarked ring has stirred buyers and sellers into unusually careful silence.","motivation":"Keep the Fog Brokers' charter intact so the market can continue managing dangerous debts in one place.","goal":"Find out who is trading information about the unmarked ring before the watch uses the panic to close the Fogmarket.","flaw":"She turns every bond into a bargain and assumes that help freely given will become a debt.","internal_conflict":"Sella wants to protect people from losing their names, but fears that acting without payment will leave her with no leverage when the market is threatened.","external_conflict":"The Parish Watch calls the brokers' name-debts extortion and may shut the market; Mara's investigation risks exposing a source Sella has promised to protect.","arc":"Sella begins by offering Mara only information in exchange for a valuable secret. When a watch patrol arrives at the Fogmarket seeking the source of the ring's rumors, Sella must choose whether to name Mara as the source or risk her own charter by redirecting the patrol. She protects Mara without demanding a debt, and ends willing to use her market's knowledge as a public safeguard rather than only as private leverage.","personality_traits":["wry","calculating","resourceful","guarded"],"abilities":[{"name":"Market listening","description":"Can piece together rumors and obligations from careful conversations with traders who would not speak openly to the watch.","category":"social"},{"name":"Debt ledger","description":"Remembers the terms and connections behind many name-debts traded under the Fog Brokers' charter.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_ada_rook","name":"Ada Rook","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_salt_chapel","description":"The Salt Chapel's registrar, Ada Rook maintains the tablets on which every citizen's name is kept against the fog. She took up the office after the death of her predecessor and has spent years repairing entries blurred by damp air and careless hands. Tall and stooped, with silver hair braided close to her head, she wears a plain apron dusted white with salt and carries a narrow slate for recording marks instead of speaking names aloud. Ada believes the registry is a promise made by the living to remember one another, not merely a safeguard against the Chiming.","motivation":"Preserve the integrity of the salt registry and the dignity of those whose names it holds.","goal":"Discover whether the unmarked ring has disturbed a registered name before the next fog reaches the chapel.","flaw":"She clings to procedure even when delay leaves people without the help they need.","internal_conflict":"Ada fears that acting on uncertain evidence will damage the registry, yet knows that silence can abandon the very citizens it exists to protect.","external_conflict":"The watch's proposed stilling order and the brokers' name-debts both threaten to make the registry a tool of control rather than communal memory.","arc":"Ada begins by refusing to alter or reveal any registry entry without a complete formal record. When Mara brings her a name-token whose salt entry has begun to blur after the strange ring, Ada must choose between waiting for official authorization and sharing what she knows before the fog arrives. She opens the relevant record to Mara and Orrin, accepting that careful cooperation is not the same as careless tampering; by the end, she keeps the registry's safeguards while making its warnings available in time to matter.","personality_traits":["patient","scrupulous","compassionate","reserved"],"abilities":[{"name":"Salt registrar","description":"Can maintain the chapel's name entries and recognize when salt, handwriting, or a citizen's token shows signs of disturbance.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Silent protocol","description":"Communicates names and instructions through established signs and written marks when fog makes speech unsafe.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_orrin","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","target_character_id":"chr_orrin_kest","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Mara Vell's effort to investigate the unmarked ring directly opposes Orrin Kest's order to still the storm-bells, forcing them to decide whether evidence or precaution should guide the parish."},{"id":"rel_orrin_mara","source_character_id":"chr_orrin_kest","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","relationship_type":"authority","description":"Orrin Kest has the power to enforce a writ against Mara Vell, while her knowledge of the bells makes her the witness he must either silence or hear."},{"id":"rel_mara_sella","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","target_character_id":"chr_sella_quill","relationship_type":"uneasy ally","description":"Sella Quill gives Mara Vell access to Fogmarket rumors, but their alliance is strained by Sella's habit of treating information as a debt."},{"id":"rel_ada_mara","source_character_id":"chr_ada_rook","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Ada Rook teaches Mara Vell how the salt registry protects names and challenges her to consider who could be harmed by keeping evidence private."},{"id":"rel_ada_orrin","source_character_id":"chr_ada_rook","target_character_id":"chr_orrin_kest","relationship_type":"opponent","description":"Ada Rook resists Orrin Kest's attempt to make the registry serve the watch's control, while he fears her caution about procedure will leave the parish exposed."}]}
