eeping","description":"Remembers the exact terms of bargains she witnesses and notices when a proposed trade leaves an obligation unclear.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_orrin_carter","name":"Orrin Carter","role":"antagonist","description":"A careful representative of the Carter Kin, Orrin grew up riding the fair’s wains and learning which lanes fold first when leap-season ends. He is broad-shouldered, soft-spoken, and usually wears a weatherproof blue waistcoat with a brass tally-hook at the belt. His family has been entrusted with the Ninth Stall’s lease, and he believes selling it is the most dependable way to settle obligations owed by the carters.","motivation":"Keep the Carter Kin’s promises manageable and protect the family from taking on more debts than it can keep.","goal":"Complete the sale of the Ninth Stall’s lease before closing day and use the trade to meet the Carter Kin’s outstanding obligations.","flaw":"He treats a workable agreement as fair even when it shuts out people with an older claim.","internal_conflict":"Orrin wants to honor his kin’s responsibilities, yet suspects that a quick sale would repeat the unfairness that put the lease in his family’s hands.","external_conflict":"Mara’s family still holds the right to claim the Ninth Stall, and the Tallykeepers may reject a sale that ignores that claim.","arc":"Orrin begins convinced that selling the lease is the safest way to settle his kin’s debts. When Mara presents a trade that could meet those obligations while honoring the family claim, he must choose between his prepared sale and a more complicated bargain. He withdraws the sale and helps put the terms before the Stallholders’ Round, learning to judge fairness by who is included, not only by whether a debt is paid.","home_location_id":"loc_leap_lane","faction_id":"fac_carters","personality_traits":["practical","reserved","dutiful","cautious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Lane lore","description":"Knows how the fair’s lanes are carried and folded, and can estimate how much time remains before the fair moves on.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Trade accounting","description":"Can quickly compare the value and timing of proposed exchanges of goods and favours.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_vesper_quill","name":"Vesper Quill","role":"supporting","description":"A Tallykeeper who records favours on wishing tags and helps judge disputes of debt. Vesper was apprenticed in the Wishing Barn and takes care to write each promise in plain language. They are a small, silver-haired person with ink-stained fingertips, round spectacles, and a mustard-yellow shawl crowded with pockets for tags, pencils, and tea samples.","motivation":"Make the fair’s promises legible and its debt rulings consistent.","goal":"Determine which favour connected to the Ninth Stall remains unsettled and rule on the claim before the third bell.","flaw":"They rely on the written record so heavily that they hesitate to consider the people and circumstances behind it.","internal_conflict":"Vesper values impartiality, but worries that strict procedure can preserve an old mistake as easily as it can prevent a new one.","external_conflict":"The Ninth Stall’s claim depends on an old unkept favour, while more favours are owed than can be kept before the fair closes.","arc":"Vesper begins the season ready to apply the old record exactly as written. After Mara and Orrin bring forward a proposed trade, Vesper checks the wishing tag against the original terms and invites both to clarify what can still be kept. They end by ruling on the claim with the record intact but the present circumstances fully considered, instead of treating procedure as a substitute for judgment.","home_location_id":"loc_wishing_barn","faction_id":"fac_tallykeepers","personality_traits":["precise","fair-minded","curious","reserved"],"abilities":[{"name":"Tally reading","description":"Can trace the wording and history of recorded favours to identify which promises remain unsettled.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Patient mediation","description":"Helps disputing merchants restate their offers in terms both sides can evaluate.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_sella_bramble","name":"Sella Bramble","role":"supporting","description":"A veteran tea merchant at the Kettle Commons and a member of the Stallholders’ Round. Sella once traded samples with Mara’s aunt and remembers the Ninth Stall before it was shuttered. She is tall and round-faced, with a braid threaded in dried apple peel and a striped apron full of tasting spoons. Her tent is known for blends that make even hurried merchants sit down for a moment.","motivation":"Keep the Kettle Commons a place where merchants exchange help as readily as goods.","goal":"Gather enough willing merchants to offer a useful, keepable trade that supports Mara’s claim without creating new unpayable favours.","flaw":"She smooths over disagreements too quickly, hoping kindness alone will make people agree.","internal_conflict":"Sella wants to preserve the Commons’ neighborly spirit, but knows avoiding a difficult conversation can leave the least powerful merchant unheard.","external_conflict":"The favour shortage leaves little time for merchants to help Mara, and the Stallholders’ Round must decide whether the proposed trade is a fair basis for the claim.","arc":"Sella begins by offering tea and encouragement while avoiding the contentious question of who should give up what. When the merchants’ samples prove too small to settle the old favour, she convenes a clear exchange of ingredients, labor, and credit that each person can keep before closing. She ends willing to let a disagreement be spoken plainly, helping the Round consider Mara’s claim on concrete terms.","home_location_id":"loc_kettle_commons","faction_id":"fac_stallholders","personality_traits":["warm","diplomatic","generous","conflict-averse"],"abilities":[{"name":"Tea tasting","description":"Recognizes the ingredients and balance of a tea blend by taste and smell.","category":"other"},{"name":"Merchant convening","description":"Brings stallholders together and helps them turn scattered offers into a practical trade.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_orrin","source_character_id":"chr_mara_thistle","target_character_id":"chr_orrin_carter","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Mara Thistle and Orrin Carter have opposing claims over the Ninth Stall: she seeks to restore her family’s right, while he is arranging a sale of its lease."},{"id":"rel_orrin_mara","source_character_id":"chr_orrin_carter","target_character_id":"chr_mara_thistle","relationship_type":"uneasy ally","description":"Orrin Carter distrusts Mara Thistle’s challenge to the sale at first, but her proposed trade gives him a way to meet his kin’s obligations while honoring her family’s claim."},{"id":"rel_vesper_mara","source_character_id":"chr_vesper_quill","target_character_id":"chr_mara_thistle","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Vesper Quill guides Mara Thistle through the wishing-tag record and urges her to make her claim in terms the Tallykeepers can fairly judge."},{"id":"rel_sella_mara","source_character_id":"chr_sella_bramble","target_character_id":"chr_mara_thistle","relationship_type":"friend","description":"Sella Bramble is Mara Thistle’s friend and trading ally, encouraging her claim and helping gather offers from the Kettle Commons."},{"id":"rel_sella_vesper","source_character_id":"chr_sella_bramble","target_character_id":"chr_vesper_quill","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Sella Bramble and Vesper Quill work together to turn the merchants’ proposed contributions into clear, keepable terms for the Tallykeepers to review."}]}
