edger hand","description":"Can compare dates, seals, and filing marks across crowded harbour records and spot inconsistencies.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Courtroom composure","description":"Can keep a measured voice while opposing claimants try to provoke or hurry her.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_yusuf_alhadi","name":"Yusuf al-Hadi","role":"supporting","description":"Yusuf al-Hadi is an envoy representing merchants from across the western sea, lodged at the Envoy House with a small delegation. He is a broad-shouldered man in his forties, with a trimmed beard silvering at the chin and a travel-worn robe carefully mended at the cuffs. Years of bargaining have made him patient in public and exacting in private; he carries a folded copy of his filing receipt inside his sash.","motivation":"Protect the merchants who entrusted him with their cargo and the season's passage.","goal":"Secure the first sailing slot for his delegation by proving its claim was filed earliest.","flaw":"He mistakes persistence for proof and can become so fixed on winning that he ignores the cost of delay.","internal_conflict":"Yusuf believes his merchants deserve fair treatment, but fears that yielding even a little will invite the court to disregard them altogether.","external_conflict":"The other two envoys dispute his filing time, and the gift scandal makes his delegation's attempts to secure favorable treatment suspect.","arc":"Yusuf begins certain that only an unyielding demand will protect his delegation. When the deadlock threatens to keep all three fleets at the port after the pilots declare the wind turned, he must choose between insisting on his private receipt or allowing Mira to compare all claims in public. He submits the receipt for scrutiny and accepts a witnessed ruling, ending still protective of his merchants but no longer willing to let pride prolong their danger.","home_location_id":"loc_envoy_house","faction_id":"fac_majlis","personality_traits":["patient","proud","measured","protective"],"abilities":[{"name":"Commercial negotiation","description":"Can read the priorities behind a bargain and frame terms that merchants may accept.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_lian_wen","name":"Lian Wen","role":"supporting","description":"Lian Wen is an envoy for a fleet whose merchants trade from the eastern reaches of the sea. She is in her late thirties, with a straight-backed bearing, a long dark braid threaded with a plain fastening, and travel clothes of fine but practical weave. Her quiet manner is often mistaken for deference; in negotiation she remembers every promise and every pause.","motivation":"Ensure her fleet is treated by the same rules as the older, better-connected delegations.","goal":"Obtain a clear, public determination of the filing order rather than accept a private arrangement.","flaw":"She withholds useful information until she is sure she can control how it will be used.","internal_conflict":"Lian wants to trust a fair hearing, but experience has taught her that transparency can expose her delegation to pressure.","external_conflict":"Her claim is challenged by Yusuf and the third envoy, while the gift scandal threatens to make every delegation's evidence appear bought.","arc":"Lian begins guarding her evidence because she expects the court to favor familiar traders. When Mira proposes a witnessed comparison, Lian must decide whether to reveal that her receipt bears a mark absent from the copies circulated at the Envoy House. She places it before the court despite the risk of scrutiny, ending more willing to share evidence when the procedure is public and reciprocal.","home_location_id":"loc_envoy_house","personality_traits":["patient","discerning","guarded","disciplined"],"abilities":[{"name":"Close observation","description":"Notices small differences in documents, seals, and the behavior of people under pressure.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_tomas_varela","name":"Tomás Varela","role":"supporting","description":"Tomás Varela is an envoy for a small fleet whose merchants cannot afford to miss the season. He is a lean man in his early forties, with sun-darkened skin, a narrow moustache, and a bright sash worn over a travel-stained coat. His charm fills a room quickly, though his quick smile rarely reveals how worried he is about the cargo waiting in the Pepper Warehouses.","motivation":"Keep his fleet's merchants solvent and prevent their cargo from sitting until the next season.","goal":"Win the first sailing slot or secure a credible ruling before the wind turns.","flaw":"He uses charm and calculated ambiguity where a direct admission would serve him better.","internal_conflict":"Tomás wants to believe he can protect his merchants without compromising his honor, but he is tempted to blur facts when the stakes feel desperate.","external_conflict":"His disputed claim is entangled with rumors of unregistered gifts, and the other envoys suspect his confidence is meant to conceal a weakness in his filing.","arc":"Tomás begins by treating the filing dispute as a contest he can win through persuasion. When Mira's inquiry reaches the gift register and his evasions risk making every claim look corrupt, he must choose between continuing to obscure a clerical mistake or acknowledging it before the court. He names the mistake and offers his receipt for comparison, ending with less leverage but a more credible claim and a clearer conscience.","home_location_id":"loc_envoy_house","personality_traits":["charming","anxious","resourceful","evasive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Persuasive address","description":"Can hold a room's attention and make a difficult proposal sound worth hearing.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_salim_bakri","name":"Salim Bakri","role":"supporting","description":"Salim Bakri is a master pilot who serves at the Pilot Ghat, where the harbour's public rite binds declarations of the turning monsoon. He is a weathered man in his fifties, with a salt-stiff beard, a sun-creased brow, and a limp from years on wet harbour steps. He speaks sparingly and studies the sea before he studies the faces waiting for his judgment.","motivation":"Protect the pilots' credibility after an earlier declaration was bought and misread.","goal":"Declare the monsoon turned only when the sea's signs support it, and ensure the public rite is observed.","flaw":"He guards his judgment so fiercely that he rarely explains what he sees until others have already drawn conclusions.","internal_conflict":"Salim knows the court needs a timely declaration, but fears that speaking under pressure will repeat the old betrayal of the ghat's oath.","external_conflict":"The rival claims have stalled the court as the season approaches its turning, while merchants and envoys press him for a declaration.","arc":"Salim begins determined to let the sea speak for itself and to offer no explanation that could be twisted. When the three envoys' deadlock threatens to outlast the sailing season, he must choose whether to keep his observations private or state them during the public rite. He explains the signs he has witnessed before declaring the turn, ending with a stronger public trust in the ghat's oath and a willingness to make his judgment intelligible.","home_location_id":"loc_pilot_ghat","personality_traits":["observant","cautious","unyielding","plain-spoken"],"abilities":[{"name":"Reading the sea","description":"Interprets wind, water, and harbour conditions to judge whether the monsoon has turned.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mira_yusuf","source_character_id":"chr_mira_das","target_character_id":"chr_yusuf_alhadi","relationship_type":"adversarial","description":"Mira must test Yusuf's claim against the ledger, while Yusuf suspects her reliance on the court's records will favor its established traders."},{"id":"rel_yusuf_lian","source_character_id":"chr_yusuf_alhadi","target_character_id":"chr_lian_wen","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Yusuf and Lian each believe their delegation filed first, and neither trusts the other's account of the disputed hour."},{"id":"rel_lian_tomas","source_character_id":"chr_lian_wen","target_character_id":"chr_tomas_varela","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Lian regards Tomás's charm and evasions as a threat to a fair comparison, while Tomás fears her careful scrutiny will expose his mistake."},{"id":"rel_mira_salim","source_character_id":"chr_mira_das","target_character_id":"chr_salim_bakri","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Mira needs Salim's timely, public declaration to close the slot dispute, and Salim trusts her to record his words faithfully."},{"id":"rel_mira_lian","source_character_id":"chr_mira_das","target_character_id":"chr_lian_wen","relationship_type":"cautious ally","description":"Lian's evidence can help Mira test the ledger, but Lian watches closely to see whether Mira gives her claim an equal hearing."}]}
